# extdir

> A community-run directory of open-source Shopware 6 extensions. {{ total }} indexed,
> with the Shopware versions each declares support for, whether anyone still maintains
> it, and what its licence permits.

Independent project, no connection to Shopware AG.

## Read this before quoting compatibility

Compatibility comes from the `shopware/core` constraint the maintainer declared in
`composer.json`. Nothing here has been installed against a running Shopware. Say
"declares support for", not "works with".

An open-ended constraint such as `^6.5` claims every later 6.x release, including ones
published after the code was last touched. The API marks these: `declaresSupportFor`
gives a tier per version, and `caret` or `wildcard` means the claim is wider than what
was tested.

## Read this before recommending an install

A public repository is not permission to redistribute. 109 of the indexed packages
declare a proprietary licence and 49 are copyleft. Check `licence.redistributable`
before telling anyone to install something.

## JSON API

- [/api](/api): what the API answers, and the two caveats above restated.
- [/api/extensions](/api/extensions): filter by `shopware`, `category`, `licence`,
  `maintenance`, `q`, `page`. Same filters and same counts as the website.
- [/api/extensions/{slug}](/api/extensions): one extension plus its compatibility matrix.

Responses are cacheable for an hour and the data changes once a night, so please cache.

## Other machine-readable endpoints

- [/repo/packages.json](/repo/packages.json): Composer v2 repository for the extensions
  Packagist does not carry. Metadata only; downloads come from the source.
- [/feed.atom](/feed.atom): newly indexed extensions.
- [/sitemap.xml](/sitemap.xml)

## Pages

- [/ranking](/ranking): the ordering formula, rendered from the constants that run it.
- [/boards](/boards): who maintains and ships the most, and what is installed most.
  Popularity is shown here and never affects ranking.
- [/about](/about), [/takedown](/takedown): what this is, and how to have an entry
  corrected or removed.

